<clause id="sec-mlb-space-objects-and-attributes" anchor="sec-mlb-space-objects-and-attributes" obligation="normative" semx-id="_d7908661-8b43-2e13-2029-a44d251c63bd">
<title id="_7f429fae-bc4e-6580-463a-f16937f58178" semx-id="_52d7531b-d0cd-7ad4-47c3-065e414020bd">MLB Space Objects and Attributes</title><fmt-title depth="2" id="_9f85895a-52d4-1b73-06b8-4387bde79a13"><span class="fmt-caption-label">3<span class="fmt-autonum-delim">.</span>4</span><span class="fmt-caption-delim"><tab/></span><semx element="title" source="_7f429fae-bc4e-6580-463a-f16937f58178">MLB Space Objects and Attributes</semx></fmt-title><fmt-xref-label><span class="fmt-element-name">Clause</span> 3<span class="fmt-autonum-delim">.</span>4</fmt-xref-label>
<p id="_8ada2f4b-d286-5899-f705-cb273ed5c5f8" semx-id="_8ada2f4b-d286-5899-f705-cb273ed5c5f8">There no MLB Space objects defined. Any Space object will need to be generated from the generic object Space and registered in the Feature Catalogue for a particular product.</p>
</clause>

<clause id="sec-mlb-generic-feature-objects-and-defining-attributes" anchor="sec-mlb-generic-feature-objects-and-defining-attributes" obligation="normative" semx-id="_d71dd79d-c297-6db0-8a2d-a63c95891119">
<title id="_bab1bb7f-2552-be21-b60b-b45a20ceb921" semx-id="_4e9d290b-53e3-0024-81c2-58a650b8bc84">MLB Generic Feature Objects and Defining Attributes</title><fmt-title depth="2" id="_7adb5fd8-4fac-fda7-eebc-52b76a9b87f9"><span class="fmt-caption-label">3<span class="fmt-autonum-delim">.</span>5</span><span class="fmt-caption-delim"><tab/></span><semx element="title" source="_bab1bb7f-2552-be21-b60b-b45a20ceb921">MLB Generic Feature Objects and Defining Attributes</semx></fmt-title><fmt-xref-label><span class="fmt-element-name">Clause</span> 3<span class="fmt-autonum-delim">.</span>5</fmt-xref-label>
<p id="_2cb5f7af-5758-0e4f-de5a-db357a04485c" semx-id="_2cb5f7af-5758-0e4f-de5a-db357a04485c">There are four generic feature object types, Location, Limit, Zone and Space. These objects serve as the root objects for all of the registered Feature Types. However these four objects may also be instantiated and specialized where there is a need to construct as special object type.  Figure 3-5 below illustrates the relationship of the generic feature objects and defining attributes.</p>

<figure id="fig-6" anchor="fig-6" semx-id="_52fd086d-470d-527f-fce4-05fd239e5cbf" autonum="3-5"><fmt-name id="_efdb6b30-c3af-dc6a-eac9-eda56e01aafd"><span class="fmt-caption-label"><span class="fmt-element-name">Figure</span> 3<span class="fmt-autonum-delim">-</span>5</span></fmt-name><fmt-xref-label><span class="fmt-element-name">Figure</span> 3<span class="fmt-autonum-delim">-</span>5</fmt-xref-label><image id="_307738c6-0939-c837-80b4-9b6b16c15129" src="/__w/mn-samples-iho/mn-samples-iho/_site/documents/s121-a/_tmp_images_14f49151-f05f-492c-bda0-687b30b9a27b/b9c11658-fb5d-4501-9d46-c3963afb79bd.png" extracted="true" mimetype="image/png" height="auto" width="auto" filename="images/image-12.png" semx-id="_307738c6-0939-c837-80b4-9b6b16c15129"/></figure>
</clause>
</clause>

<clause id="sec-feature-catalogue-entries" anchor="sec-feature-catalogue-entries" obligation="normative" semx-id="_956f2ab3-333b-1550-2e57-968a85082021" displayorder="8">
<title id="_dad3f97e-054b-6c38-d5dc-b2a492230c4f" semx-id="_51821d3b-dcfa-fb83-f219-97c4091f7fee">Feature Catalogue Entries</title><fmt-title depth="1" id="_f2262b35-1844-3fa5-f100-128e2013bddb"><span class="fmt-caption-label">4</span><span class="fmt-caption-delim"><tab/></span><semx element="title" source="_dad3f97e-054b-6c38-d5dc-b2a492230c4f">Feature Catalogue Entries</semx></fmt-title><fmt-xref-label><span class="fmt-element-name">Section</span> 4</fmt-xref-label>
<p id="_2a210d88-1b80-21e5-7eb0-71c134190e7b" semx-id="_2a210d88-1b80-21e5-7eb0-71c134190e7b">The objects and attributes identified for use in the S-121 Product Specification are described in conformance with the IHO Geospatial Information (GI) Registry.<note id="_e91da4d9-1a39-7dd7-6cba-88035f7fb526" semx-id="_e91da4d9-1a39-7dd7-6cba-88035f7fb526" autonum=""><fmt-name id="_c01fe468-3378-5a8e-c84e-0446bb9f70ab"><span class="fmt-caption-label"><span class="fmt-element-name">NOTE</span></span><span class="fmt-label-delim"><tab/></span></fmt-name><fmt-xref-label><span class="fmt-element-name">Note</span></fmt-xref-label><fmt-xref-label container="sec-feature-catalogue-entries"><span class="fmt-xref-container"><span class="fmt-element-name">Section</span> 4</span><span class="fmt-comma">,</span> <span class="fmt-element-name">Note</span></fmt-xref-label><p id="_c08d20e2-3bd9-bd5f-71fd-9ff662139a1f" semx-id="_c08d20e2-3bd9-bd5f-71fd-9ff662139a1f">In this version 1.0.0 of the S-121 Product Specification the following tables constitute the Feature Catalogue as a document. These tables will then be entered into the IHO GI Registry and a subsequent version of the Feature Catalogue will be generated from the Registry. These tables in a subsequent version of the S-121 Product Specification will also be generated from the Registry. This process ensures complete alignment between the Feature Catalogue, the Registry and this document.</p>
</note></p>



