<td id="_084f64c3-354b-2170-3f30-63caa962e126" valign="top" align="left" semx-id="_084f64c3-354b-2170-3f30-63caa962e126"><p id="_84fe969e-0229-9ce0-d63f-afb93fb1182f" semx-id="_84fe969e-0229-9ce0-d63f-afb93fb1182f">A “Space” is an object of 2 dimensions with a height description located in 2 or 3 dimensional “Space”. This is sometimes called 2 1/2 dimensions. A “Space” has the same geometry as a “Zone” with the attributes of vertical position. The vertical position may be explicit numerical attributes of height above a reference or a textual description.</p>
</td>
</tr><tr id="_dad6d4c1-f494-9925-a947-9ad11b2d40c0" semx-id="_dad6d4c1-f494-9925-a947-9ad11b2d40c0"><th id="_fe9273f9-6500-6dff-3012-1894751978dc" valign="top" align="left" semx-id="_fe9273f9-6500-6dff-3012-1894751978dc"><strong>Permitted Primitives:</strong></th>
