<td id="_96b83ed7-1e00-a57a-3a33-febceb48f9df" valign="top" align="left" semx-id="_96b83ed7-1e00-a57a-3a33-febceb48f9df"/></tr><tr id="_0b7ea41c-969c-e039-867d-b7d29868f389" semx-id="_0b7ea41c-969c-e039-867d-b7d29868f389"><th id="_db01fedc-7156-3a17-5041-46d72677271d" valign="top" align="left" semx-id="_db01fedc-7156-3a17-5041-46d72677271d"><strong>Remarks:</strong></th>
<td id="_01629edd-a0a2-c425-0046-5d1857c538bc" valign="top" align="left" semx-id="_01629edd-a0a2-c425-0046-5d1857c538bc"><p id="_3edbc911-78f9-1a21-9232-832d18c3eb5b" semx-id="_3edbc911-78f9-1a21-9232-832d18c3eb5b">Realized from ISO 19152 LADM “LA_GroupParty” which stereotypes this object as a “featureType”. Since it is not a feature in the same sense as the term feature is used in IHO S-100, the stereotype has been removed. LA_GroupParty describes  any number of parties, forming together a distinct entity, with each party registered. Since LA_GroupParty is a subtype of LA_Party this is described as a single class “Party” that includes a conditional attribute “partyGroupTypeList” that defines the type of a group party.</p>
</td>
</tr></tbody>
</table>
</clause>

